  "_comment": [
    "Grouped rows exactly as the Analytics Engine SQL API returns them, keyed by",
    "the query ids scripts/signals-rollup/queries.ts assigns. Numbers are STRINGS",
    "on 2026-09-16 and real numbers on 2026-09-17, because the API returns strings",
    "and the rollup must not care either way.",
    "",
    "2026-09-16 is a busy day built to hit every branch of the floor: an",
    "install-gated value with a large n and a tiny gate (duel format limited: 120",
    "duels from 9 installs), complementary suppression on most dimensions, a",
    "dimension with nothing folded at all (heartbeat platform), a cross row whose",
    "result split is entirely null (opponentId marsh-mother), a cross row that",
    "publishes its split whole (difficulty medium), and a LITERAL value named",
    "'other' that is real data (settings.renderScale, a real member of",
    "SignalRenderScale) and must never be confused with the fold bucket.",
    "",
    "2026-09-17 is a quiet day: all three day gates close, and the run still writes",
    "a file with three nulls so the gap in the series is explained.",
    "",
    "chrome-broodmother's 137 duels are a deliberately distinctive number, so the",
    "logger test can prove a sub-floor count never reaches a line of output."
